+## Review
+
+Twelve findings of the reviewers and the build's four open points, each settled with a test written against the code
+as it was (`CreaturesReviewGameTests`: all but the charge fail on the commit before these fixes, the charge on
+ef61de1^; `tools/dev/animcheck.sh`: all four checks fail on the old animator) or with pictures
+(`/home/user/shots/CREATURES1B`: `review/`, `fight/`, `strips/`, `sw/`). Commits: eceeac9 (server: releases, the split, the watched grab, crumbs; the game tests), dd60cd5 (animator: the frozen
+pose, the head, deaths of another kind; animcheck), 2c2b41d (clips and art: loops, the thumb, the heckler, elites),
+30b5655 (the Rat King's blow), f2feb01 and db9f518 (proof scripts, `sstrip`).
+
+- **F1 the bunny's copies before its pinch** (motion, wrong): fixed (eceeac9, db9f518). A kind that splits in its death clip splits at
+  the clip's pop (`Deaths.splitTick`: the last tick of the death), the halves start small with their spawn clip and hop
+  apart, one to each side, out of a small puff. Test `dustBunnySplitsAtItsPop`; pictures `fight/fight1b_bunny_split_*`
+  (the pinch, then the halves), `strips/dust_bunny_death.png`.
+- **F2 loops with too few keys** (motion, rough): fixed (2c2b41d) at the cause: `anim.loop` compares its keys with the poses
+  half-way between and refuses keys that flatten a wave (strict for the Understage's plans, a warning elsewhere). It found
+  the four named and four more of part 1a: the stage rat's jaw, the lurker's fangs, the Gaffer's point and thumb, the
+  Rat King's jaw in his rage and act three. All now have enough keys and move (`ratking idle whiskers` three key values
+  instead of one zero, the understudy's hands and forearms, the bunny's tuft and its stun squash). Proof: the build
+  (`python3 tools/content/mob/anim.py`), `sw/*_idle.png`. Arcade Zero and the Sun Tomb have loops it warns about
+  (glitch, hitbox, fan, masher, cursor, scarab, disc): left to their lane.
+- **F3 heckler like the rat wrangler** (motion, wrong): fixed (2c2b41d). A pear of a man: short legs, a belly wider than his
+  shoulders, a bobble hat with a pompom instead of the flat cap, a tomato ready at his shoulder (idle) and the bag held
+  out. Overlap as black shapes, aligned at the feet (`render.py`, three-quarter view): heckler/rat wrangler 0.73 -> 0.60
+  at rest, 0.61 in his idle; from the side about 0.5 before and after; his nearest is now the prompter at 0.64 (others
+  among the humanoids 0.69, the reviewer's figure for the next pair). Pictures
+  `silhouettes_understage_review.png`, `lineup_ten.png`, `heckler.png`.
+- **F4 the thumb's whole turn inside the clip** (motion, rough): fixed (2c2b41d); the thumb comes back up the way it went (largest
+  step at 60 fps 11 deg, was 327 deg), and the build refuses a key that turns a part back by a whole turn inside a clip.
+- **F5 proof pictures** (motion, rough): fixed (f2feb01, db9f518). `sw/` holds the software strips of every clip of the six kinds (103);
+  the tour films the understudy from a spectator (who does not count as watching) so its walk, run, habits, attack,
+  stun and spawn are its own, then its real frozen pose when the camera becomes a crawler (`strips/understudy_*`); the
+  fight script shows both bosses from the crawler's eyes in the open middle of a cleared room: the wind-up, the step out
+  of the mark, the whole death scene. Deaths are strips on the server's clock (`sstrip`: the server frozen and stepped
+  between pictures), so no body vanishes in the middle of its scene. Looked at frame by frame.
+- **F6 the tomato and the helpers before the gesture** (breaks, wrong): fixed (eceeac9). What comes out of a gesture comes at its
+  clip's contact (`Blows.RELEASE`, `mob_blows.py RELEASE`): the heckler's and Grandmother Lint's throws at 8 ticks, the
+  Rat King's rats on the third bang (17), Grandmother Lint's grandchildren on her call (14), and the same for part 1a's
+  wrangler (15) and Eternal Understudy (17); a daze in between breaks it, no blow starts over it. Tests
+  `tomatoFliesAtTheThrowsRelease`, `dazeBreaksAThrowBeforeItsRelease`, `ratsComeOnTheThirdBang`,
+  `clipsCoverReleasesAndElites` (clip contact = server release).
+- **F7 frozen mid-grab finishes the grab** (breaks, wrong): fixed (eceeac9, dd60cd5) on both sides: watched, the server breaks the grab and
+  ends its motion; the client snaps into the frozen pose in 0.12 s and drops the action. Test
+  `watchedUnderstudyDropsItsGrab`; animcheck `frozen breaks the grab` (star pose 0.17 s after freezing, was 0.67 s);
+  picture `fight/fight1b_understudy_freeze_*`.
+- **F8 head snap and star pose at a death or stun** (breaks, rough): fixed (dd60cd5); the frozen pose yields to a stun and to the
+  death, and the head is drawn with the look's weight. animcheck `frozen yields to the death` (largest head step 3.4
+  deg per frame, was 28; forearm_l follows the death, was 71 deg off); picture `strips/understudy_death.png` (killed
+  while watched).
+- **F9 stale head angle on a second client** (breaks, rough): fixed (dd60cd5) at the cause: nothing of the head is kept on the
